{
  "_README": {
    "purpose": "Curated asset dictionary for normalize/programs.py. Maps the many strings CT.gov contains for one drug onto a single canonical asset, so that (sponsor, asset) pairs can be counted as programs.",

    "why_curated_and_not_inferred": "Decision 5 in docs/SCOPE-v2.md: the LLM translates, Python decides. Asset identity determines every headline count in the landscape, so it has to be reproducible and inspectable rather than a model's judgment that varies between runs. This file is the inspectable part.",

    "why_an_allowlist_beats_stem_matching": "Learned from the corpus. Stem-matching on 'azole' looked obviously correct and put omeprazole, esomeprazole, rabeprazole, lansoprazole, pantoprazole, metronidazole, tinidazole, sulfamethoxazole, letrozole and anastrozole into the antifungal asset list -- PPIs, a nitroimidazole antiparasitic, a sulfonamide, and two aromatase inhibitors. Two of those were in the top 30 'antifungal' interventions by count. There is no clean shared suffix across antifungal azoles (fluconazole, clotrimazole, bifonazole) that excludes the others, so an allowlist is not a shortcut here, it is the only correct approach.",

    "development_codes": "Code names are the whole point of this file, not a nicety. A novel asset's early trials name it only by code -- APX001, F901318, SCY-078, CD101, VT-1161, PC945 -- and those are precisely the trials a competitive landscape most needs to catch. v1's ingest discarded them entirely; resolving them to their compound is what turns them into a visible program.",

    "active_moieties": "manogepix is the active moiety of the prodrug fosmanogepix, and both appear as interventions. They are ONE program: a sponsor developing fosmanogepix is not also competing with itself via manogepix. Same for fosravuconazole/ravuconazole.",

    "formulation_note": "Amphotericin B formulations are kept as SEPARATE assets. Conventional deoxycholate, liposomal (AmBisome), lipid complex (Abelcet), and oral encochleated (MAT2203) have materially different toxicity, route, and commercial positioning -- treating them as one asset would merge a 1960s generic with an active development program. This is a deliberate exception to 'same molecule, same asset', and it is the kind of call that should be visible in a config rather than buried in code.",

    "class_field": "Mechanistic class, used for the landscape's grouping and for the 'target' attribute in the comparison table. Populated from this dictionary, so the comparison cell renders with source='alias_dictionary' rather than 'derived_from_text' -- see the attribute_provenance table."
  },

